All four competencies covered. Summary of the authored tasks:

1. **`bracken-river`** (C-66174de0 — R runtime): air-gapped workstation where R is absent; agent must `dpkg -i` a vendored 59-deb offline closure, expose `Rscript` on PATH + in the launcher's `settings.json`, leave an idempotent `/app/setup_r.sh`, and run the R pipeline (verified on hidden seed/n/µ/σ parameter sets against an independent R recomputation).

2. **`larch-vane`** (C-69755486 — exec bit + listing preservation): three-stage acoustic-deployment pipeline shipped with all exec bits stripped; the chain entry point invokes stages directly so the bits are load-bearing; scripts are pristine-sha-checked and the `find -printf '%p %s\n'` tree listing must regenerate byte-for-byte identical; hidden recording dirs re-run the chain. (One fix during verification: `%P` → `%p`, since GNU find's `%P` strips the starting-point name.)

3. **`kiln-anchor`** (C-1a4b2841 — binary on PATH): agent authors a C gauge-log CLI, compiles to `/app/dist/kilnstat`, and installs it for bare-name invocation from any directory (verifier runs from `/tmp` via `sh -c` and recompiles the source deliverable); hidden logs probe strict clock bounds, junk tokens, exponent forms, zero-valid and missing-file cases.

4. **`myrtle-canyon`** (C-5ede2c22 — MuJoCo fresh install, plugin-free tuned model): box ships with no MuJoCo, only a pinned offline wheelhouse (`mujoco==3.2.4`); agent installs with `--no-index`, tunes a slider feed-stage model (single slide joint + motor, no plugins/assets/includes, `nplugin==0`), keeps `ref-model.xml` byte-identical to the pristine copy, and passes the 2 s sweep acceptance (tuned > 0.35 m, ref < 0.10 m) on visible + hidden drives.

